From 1c2c9b95ab0bc2b12262ef4bb6d588e707f6e8fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shloksharmawork <250544143+shloksharmawork@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:41:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(poh): drop the PyYAML dependency that broke CI

The proof-of-humanity round imported PyYAML, which is in neither
requirements-ci.txt nor the runtime path, so tests/test_poh.py failed at
collection and took every build-qtop and coverage-qtop job down with it
(the advisory poh job passed only because its workflow pip-installed
pyyaml itself).

CONTRIBUTING.md asks contributors to avoid dependencies, and poh/claims.yaml
only uses a small yaml subset, so tools/poh.py now carries its own stdlib
reader and writer:

- yaml_load / yaml_dump handle block mappings, lists of mappings, scalars
  and comments; flow style, anchors and broken quoting raise YamlError
  instead of being silently mis-parsed
- tests cover the subset, the round trip, the rejections, and a real parse
  of the committed poh/claims.yaml
- tools/poh.py is reformatted so 'ruff format --check' passes

.github/workflows/poh.yml can now drop its 'pip install pyyaml' step.

make github-ci, make coverage-xml and make compat-py36 all pass locally:
272 tests, 0 failures.

